inscriptions.inscription:
7 seals of Qianlong emperor  (r. 1736–95): 

Gu xi tian zi 古希天子; 
Shou 壽; 
Qianlong jian shang 乾隆鑑賞; 
San xi tang jing jian xi 三希堂精鑑璽; 
Yi zi sun 宜子孫; 
Tai shang huang di zhi bao 太上皇帝之寳; 
Qian qing gong bao 乾清宮寶.

6 seals of Cheng Qi 程琦 (1911–1988): 

Ke an geng zi wu shi yi hou suo de ming ji 可菴庚子五十以後所得名跡; 
5 other Cheng Qi seals.

4 colophons and 24 additional seals: 

1 colophon, dated 1811, and 5 seals of Xiang Yuan 項源 (active about 1811); 
1 colophon, dated 1858, and 2 seals of Qi Junzao 祁寯藻 (1793-1866); 
1 colophon and 4 seals of Zhang Yunzhong 張允中 (1881–1960?); 
4 seals of Jiang Xun 江恂 (active about 1753–after 1780); 
1 colophon dated 1943, and 2 seals of Wang Shaoming 汪兆銘 (Wang Jingwei 汪精衛, 1883–1944); 
1 seal of Qi Zhiliu 祁之鏐 (active about 1858); 
2 seals of Yu Zhimeng 俞芷盟 (second half of 19th century); 
4 seals unidentified.

Section A (Chrysanthemums): 
1 poem and 1 seal of Zhang Yuanzhen 張元禎 (1437–1507) - Jinshi, 1461; 
1 poems and 3 seals of Ni Yue 倪岳 (1444–1501) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 2 seals of Zhao Xiang 趙祥 (life dates unknown) - Jinshi, 1469; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Wu Xixian 吳希賢 (1437–1489) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Lü Chang 呂㦂 (1449–1511) - Juren, 1471; 
1 poems and 3 seals of Fu Han 傅瀚 (1435–1502) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Feng Jue 馮珏 (life dates unknown) - Jinshi, 1478.

Section B (Cabbage): 
1 poem and 1 seal of Cai Qi 蔡圻 (life dates unknown) - degree information not known; 
1 poems and 3 seals of Ni Yue 倪岳 (1444–1501) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poem and 3 seals of Jiao Fang 焦芳 (1436–1517) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poem and 3 seals of Li Dongyang 李東陽 (1447–1516) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Wu Xixian, signed “Xixian” 吳希賢 - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 3 seals of Fu Han 傅瀚 (1435–1502) - Jinshi, 1464; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Lü Chang 呂㦂 (1449–1511) - Juren, 1471; 
1 poems and 2 seals of Zhao Xiang 趙祥 (life dates unknown) - Jinshi, 1469; 
1 poems and 1 seals of Feng Jue 馮珏 (life dates unknown) - Jinshi, 1478.

3 additional seals: 

1 of Pang Yuanji 龐元濟 (1864–1949); 
2 unidentified.

5 additional seals: 

2 of Xu Weiren 徐渭仁(1788－1855); 
2 of Sun Zutong 孫祖同 (1894–1937); 
1 of C. C. Wang 王季遷 (1907–2003).

1 colophon and 9 additional seals: 

3 seals of Dai Zhi 戴植 (active about 1821–1850); 
1 colophon, dated 1914, and 3 seals of Yan Shiqing 顏世清 (1873–1929); 
3 seals of Wang Nanping 王南屏 (1924–1985).

Urdu inscription at top, in nasta‘liq script:
sheep;

Hindi inscription under left corner of painting, in devanagari script:
Shri 6;

Hindi inscription below painting, in devanagari script:
2, sheep;

Hindi inscription, bottom center, in devanagari script:
674
